# Do not edit the instructor's files

The `module1_PROLOG/` through `module5_alienmoon/` trees are submitted
coursework. Two of their files contain the defects this lab exists to
document, so editing them destroys the evidence and the assignment at once.

Treat them as read-only. All work goes in `lab/`.

To study a defective program, transcribe it into `lab/02_cobol/` under a new
name and change one thing at a time, so each captured artifact isolates a
single variable.

## Never write outside this repository

A parallel session owns the Obsidian vault at
`Remote_Sync_V.01/Spaces/Work/.../COBOL & Legacy Systems/`, including a
gitignored viewing copy of this repo at `COBOL & Legacy Systems/COBOL-main/`.

Vault files are read-only reference. Read them to learn what evidence is
needed; hand results back as files under `lab/03_forensics/`. Writing to the
vault from here causes the two sessions to collide.

## Claims must cite captured output

Do not state a figure in a write-up that no artifact backs. Add it to
`make verify` so prose and evidence cannot drift apart.
